  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 28

Iteration 27 named this: remove `back-edge?` against the suite
evidence, or keep it. This file takes the removal. It is also the
largest remaining whole-pipeline performance lever that is not a
new export.

Do not overwrite 04-27.

## What remaining performance actually is

Already taken. Do not redo:

- Pool growth (iteration 06): kernel_wide 9.10x LLVM became 1.62x
- Proportional spill (iteration 07): kernel_deep 7.87x became 1.44x
- Fuel / ISA hoist (11-13). Identity leftover was strcmp
- Leaf vs LLVM (14): 5.85 / 5.80 ns = 1.009x. perfgate refused
- Scanner for call+if (16): 24-live 99 slots became 17
- Call+loop encodings, kexe, spill, suite (22-27). Production was
  still all-vreg whenever `back-edge?` was true

This iteration. Production call+loop no longer spills every vreg:

- count-loop: `[:all-vregs 8]` became `[:call-live 0]`
- pressure-loop: production `:call-live` (AArch64 full pool still
  does not measure a spill; scratch-only does)

Not this week's timing, and not a ranking:

- wide/deep leftover 1.44-1.62x is instruction selection on leaves,
  not all-vreg. fused-srem / extra MOV / FMA / PGO / kototama
  optimizer are refused
- cfg-liveness is correctness for shapes textual last-uses cannot
  see, not the first performance knob
- packing / CARv2 / kexe loader are round-trips, not ns/call
- self-tail past the fuel prologue (iteration 05) is a different
  export
- rematching leaf vs LLVM
- a timed `bench` export

The first *timed* claim this path can still make is call+loop
production vs the old all-vreg policy, on quiet judah, through
perfgate. Iteration 07: every ratio in that file is from a leaf.
Iteration 16 named the 24-live pair. That is Next, not this file.

## What landed

`allocate-with-policy` no longer short-circuits
`(and calls? (back-edge?))` to all-vreg. The scanner is the
production path. Leftover pressure still falls back via
`:spill-required`. `back-edge?` remains in source as the last-uses
hazard; it is not a routing guard. `:cfg-liveness` is still false.

ADR 0012 contract: `:back-edge` and `:loops-with-calls` are
`:call-live`. `:fallbacks` is `#{:register-pressure}`.

Pin chain (amu does not depend on kotoba-mir directly):

- kotoba-mir `767d3c0b418f85d1d177f78b0648c106a79bfb62`
- kotoba-native `4bb08b9228bc41168ab42bf6d7d2e60150104aff`
  (deps pin of mir; encodings suite 170/2212/0)
- amu `27d69898aca60db492d2c415eae31d7a72a07243`
  (deps-lock mir `767d3c0`, native `4bb08b9`)

amu tests: production count-loop `[:call-live 0]` both ISAs;
pressure-loop production `:call-live`; scratch-only still asserts
`pos?` spill-store/load. Execution oracles unchanged.

## What this is not

Not a ns/call ranking. Encodings and kexe are not perfgate.

Not LLVM beaten. Leaf refusal (14) stands. Call+loop has never
been timed against LLVM.

Not cfg-liveness. last-uses are still textual.

Not a claim that the 138-namespace suite was re-run after the
aggregate-abi pin-string fix. The 1 fail on that run *was* the
pin string. The two namespaces that encode this change are green
(23/754/0). 87 errors are the judah wasm-tools baseline.

