## Meta-review

- **The largest remaining allocator lever was spilling every vreg
  on call+loop.** That path is now `:call-live`.
- **Amu would not have seen the mir change without the native pin.**
  deps-lock is the classpath that runs.
- **The aggregate-abi pin-assert is part of bumping native.** It is
  not an allocator regression.

## Next

Time production call+loop (count-loop, and/or the iteration-16
24-live pair) against the old all-vreg policy on quiet judah.
Judge is min ns/call. Seal only via `kotoba-lang/perfgate`. Do not
overwrite 04-27. Do not rematch leaf vs LLVM. Do not claim LLVM
beaten. Do not implement cfg-liveness as a drive-by of a timing
run. Do not ship a timed `bench` export."}]
